# ML Models
data/models/
backend/data/ml_models/*.joblib
# ...but ship the small trained models so ML endpoints work in prod.
# regime.joblib / regime_features.joblib are tracked too: without them the
# deployed instance had no regime model at all and app/ml/serving.py fell back
# to replaying a frozen current_stress_prob out of metrics.joblib as if it were
# live model output. Ship the model or report the signal as unavailable —
# never both-and-pretend.
!backend/data/ml_models/lead_time.joblib
!backend/data/ml_models/feature_cols.joblib
!backend/data/ml_models/metrics.joblib
!backend/data/ml_models/regime.joblib
!backend/data/ml_models/regime_features.joblib

# MLflow local tracking store + artifacts (P5)
backend/mlruns/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# Playwright MCP artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Screenshots / test artifacts
test-screenshots/
/*.png
/Screenshot*.png

# Claude Code local state (personal) — agent memory, agent definitions, settings.
# CLAUDE.md forbids committing anything under .claude/. Until 2026-09-01 only
# .claude/skills/ was ignored, so agent-memory dirs left the tree permanently dirty —
# which made every generated artifact stamp provenance.git.dirty = true and turned that
# flag into unfalsifiable noise. Ignoring the whole directory restores the flag's meaning.
# NOTE: 9 files under .claude/ are still TRACKED from before this rule; .gitignore does not
# untrack them. See docs/OUTSTANDING_WORK.md — untracking them is an open owner decision.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md

# Personal research notes
backend/apimcpresearch.txt

# Superpowers brainstorming visual companion
.superpowers/

# UI gate run artifacts (frontend/scripts/ui-gate.cjs writes beside itself)
frontend/scripts/gate-shots/
frontend/scripts/gate-report.json
